Section 3: WIPO Diplomatic Treaty on IP, Genetic Resources and Associated TK (May 2024)

Adopted by consensus at the WIPO Diplomatic Conference in Geneva (May 24, 2024):
Article 3 — Mandatory Disclosure Requirement:
1. Patent applicants are required to disclose the country of origin of the genetic resources if the claims in a patent application are materially based on genetic resources;
2. Where the claims are materially based on traditional knowledge associated with genetic resources, applicants must disclose the indigenous peoples or local community who provided the traditional knowledge;
3. Information sharing systems: Contracting parties are mandated to establish digital information systems (databases of genetic resources and traditional knowledge, modeled after India's TKDL) in consultation with local communities, accessible to patent examiners worldwide to prevent wrongful patent grants.
